Z||000005||Cheever3000||08-28-2001||10:45 PM||||There's a lot of them on the road that are in rough shape.  They may have formed their opinions based on seeing those.  There are still many being well maintained however.  Show me any car that old with as many miles as a lot of us have, that by the same percentage of total numbers manufactured are in such good condition.  <P>Just say what those kids say on the Apple Jacks commercial: "We just <I>like</I> em, okay?"<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||tgowens||08-28-2001||10:52 PM||||While the Fiero was originally designed as a low cost commuter car there is nothing "cheap" about it. It was designed to be fuel efficient and safe. During the five year production run of the Fiero it ranked number 2 in safety tests. Second only to Volvo and ranking higher than the Mercedes and BMW. The hood, for example, is designed to buckle in the middle in a head-on collision rather than flying back and breaking the windshield.<P>The space frame which surrounds the entire passenger compartment is completely steel, the body panels are Enduroflex and Polyurathane and are designed to be "forgiving" (no dents on a Fiero - can't say that for most of the other cars on the road!) - there is an absorbant material behind the front and rear fascia to absorb the impact in a collision.......All in all, I don't think the ones you talk to know much about the Fiero!<P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero/index.html" TARGET=_blank><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennocks_sig.jpg"> </A>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Galen||08-28-2001||11:04 PM||||the same design as the Saturns if I'm not mistaken, if I am plz correct me  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Are saturns a POS?<P>------------------<BR>Ray -      <A HREF="mailto:galen@ezrpg.com">galen@ezrpg.com</A>      - <A HREF="http://www.fierolinks.f2s.com/" TARGET=_blank>www.FieroLinks.f2s.com</A> - AIM: GalenRPG - ICQ: 98668558||||reg||1
Z||000008||fiero56||08-29-2001||12:02 AM||||I can't remember the last time someone said something negative about the Fiero, all I get are positive remarks about the Fiero in general, and about mine.<P>I just thought of the last time someone made a negative comment. Some dick-head used car salesman made a crack about all Fieros(and I want to buy a car from you why?) while I was on his lot with my Fiero! My friend was considering buying a car from him that day when he made the comment. My friend was as disgusted as I was, and we left w/out buying anything. I wonder why the used car sales asked why he wasn't interested in the cars on his lot anymore?<P>I think Fiero is structurally better than most cars even produced today. My Fieros have fewer squeaks/rattles than even most of todays new cars. ||||reg||1
