Z||000011||tgowens||08-29-2001||06:11 AM||||Galen, while the Saturn <I>may</I> be the same basic design, the commonality which is shared by both cars is only in the fact that the machinery used to manufacture the Fiero was sent to the Saturn plant in TN after the Fiero plant in MI was closed.........as such, the Saturn is manufactured in the same way as the Fiero was, utilizing a "space frame" design - other than that, there is no similarity....||||reg||1
