Z||000013||2birds||08-30-2001||12:01 AM||||I just spent about 3 weeks driving my 94 Mustang GT or my 97 T-bird, because of a little exhaust leak and cylinder head repair on my 170,000 mile 86 GT.  <P>While both Fords are much newer, more comfortable (leather seats and real air conditioning instead of my worn out cloth  seats and 3X70 air conditioning in the fiero), definitely faster (both are 200+HP V-8's), and handle fairly well despite their size and weight (with a little aftermarket help for the 'bird), the feeling I have when I'm driving my Fiero is one of everything is right with the world.  <P>Maybe its because I've had the Fiero longer than I've been married (over 13 years now), or that I've driven almost every mile myself.<BR>It just feels right.<P>Either that or I need to get professional help fast...<BR>||||reg||1
